        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. In Lebanon, some schools choose to stay open despite the war Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 11:53 In Lebanon, despite ongoing strikes and insecurity, some schools have chosen to remain open. In Beirut, a school located near the southern suburbs regularly targeted continues to welcome students, while others attend classes remotely. How do you teach and learn amidst a war? FRANCE 24's Serge Berberi and Renée Davis went to meet parents and students - and found some answers. US ramps up military presence in the Middle East amid reported talks 25/03/2026 Middle East US sends 15-point peace plan to Iran while deploying troops in the region 25/03/2026 Middle East 'The humanitarian crisis here is worsening by the minute': Israel continues to bomb Lebanon 25/03/2026 Middle East US to deploy elite army brigade to Middle East: reports 24/03/2026 Middle East Pakistan’s prime minister says his nation is ready to facilitate talks to end Iran war 24/03/2026 Middle East Saudi leader said to be pushing Trump to continue war in Iran, New York Times reports 24/03/2026 Middle East War on Iran: 'Fought on faulty assumptions, notion of externally delivered regime change delusional' 24/03/2026 Middle East Tension rises between Israel and Lebanon as IDF occupies south of Litani river 24/03/2026 Middle East Iran strikes put in question US-Israeli attacks's impact on military capabilities 24/03/2026 Middle East"
